WHAT THIS PROJECT DIRECTORY CONTAIN

In the main folder you find the root_to_webN.C file, which is the main script. This produces the HTML report, the plots and animations of the project.

You also find the data stored in a root file "fmri_val1_t42.root", as well as the finished animations as .gifs and images as .pngs.

The index.html is the report. To render the LaTeX properly, open with webserver (see below).

There are three folders inside this directory. Here is a list of what they contain:
- scripts_conversion_of_data: scripts to convert the raw NifTy data file --> CSV file --> ROOT. Note that the raw data was not included to save space.
- scripts_plotting: Three scripts creating different kinds of 2D histograms and animations. If you run these scripts in ROOT you can choose you own input variable.
- Scripts_plotting_edited_for_web: IGNORE. These are the same plots as above, however modified for plugging in into the root_to_webN.C file. These are not meant to be run by the user.

--------------------
PRODUCING THE HTML REPORT

This project is produced by writing:
make
in the terminal from the main project folder. This will run the ROOT_to_webN.C file that produces the HTML report and the plots/animations.

OBS: This takes a couple of minutes to run, as there are a lot of plots to draw.

--------------------
VIEW THE REPORT
To view the report, run the following in the terminal:

python3 -http.server 8000
firefox http://127.0.0.1:8000/


-------------------
VIEWING THE PLOTS INDIVIDUALLY AND CHOOSE YOUR OWN Z-VALUES

The original scripts for plotting can be found in the folder "scrips_plotting"
- plot_2Dhist.C
- scroll_slices.C
- plot_time_ev_2D.C

If you run these in ROOT, you can decide which brain slice to look at by typing a z-value in the terminal. Remember to add an even number 0-78. The root file is added into this folder as well as the main folder for convenience. 